  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes QEA‑FAD, a variational quantum autoencoder framework for anomaly detection. On the Breast Cancer Wisconsin dataset (569 samples), the proposed ansatz achieves about 0.9 accuracy using a fidelity threshold of 0.845, outperforming two reproduced QAE baselines (0.24 and 0.81 accuracy). On the credit card fraud dataset (284,807 transactions), the model achieves compression fidelity ≈0.89 for normal transactions and ≈0.66 for fraudulent ones, with experiments run on simulators, IBM Guadalupe, and Rigetti Aspen‑11 QPUs.",
